From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:38:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Reject malformed miner settings before startup

---
 miner/V2-MINING.md                    |  9 ++-
 miner/lotus-miner-cli/src/main.rs     |  1 +
 miner/lotus-miner-gui/src/app.rs      | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++------
 miner/lotus-miner-lib/src/lib.rs      |  7 ++-
 miner/lotus-miner-lib/src/settings.rs | 53 ++++++++++++++++--
 5 files changed, 122 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/miner/V2-MINING.md b/miner/V2-MINING.md
index 822de5c9..9df36706 100644
--- a/miner/V2-MINING.md
+++ b/miner/V2-MINING.md
@@ -3,9 +3,12 @@
 The current miner has an explicit `--protocol=v1|v2` setting. V1 is the default.
 CLI V2 selection exits before GPU setup or any RPC request with a clear
 unsupported error. The GUI displays the error without starting mining, including
-when V2 was saved in its settings. The V2 P04 CPU primitive and OpenCL work/BlockID kernel are implemented
-and checked against independent vectors. The OpenCL code is available only
-through bounded library batches, not through the network miner.
+when V2 was saved in its settings. The V2 P04 CPU primitive and OpenCL
+work/BlockID kernel are implemented and checked against independent vectors.
+The OpenCL code is available only through bounded library batches, not through
+the network miner.
+Malformed numeric settings also produce CLI errors or a GUI error panel before
+server, OpenCL device or RPC initialization.
 
 ## Protocol contract
 
diff --git a/miner/lotus-miner-cli/src/main.rs b/miner/lotus-miner-cli/src/main.rs
index 952052ce..c85530d0 100644
--- a/miner/lotus-miner-cli/src/main.rs
+++ b/miner/lotus-miner-cli/src/main.rs
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ fn validate_cli_config(config: &ConfigSettings) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error
     if config.protocol == Protocol::V2 {
         return Err(V2_UNAVAILABLE.into());
     }
+    config.validate()?;
     if config.mine_to_address.is_empty() {
         return Err("V1 mining requires mine_to_address".into());
     }
